plan_mode: approved
plan_resume_context: "Post-organization checkpoint 2026-08-15: 2,496 items; graph has 12,301 deduplicated edges, one connected acyclic component, 12 layers, zero findings, and 100 percent active outcome reachability. Canonical programmes now contain detailed designs for noun-verb command consolidation, session token economics and recoverable bounded reads, SDK-first provenance, adaptive context ranking, append-only time travel, deterministic multi-agent merge, decentralized federation, recursive improvement, RL/eval environments, recurrence-derived CI, and long-horizon outcomes through 2036. New issue pm-k9m6wc uniquely owns GitHub immutable-release enforcement after live isImmutable:false evidence. Scheduled reliability pm-e70zh5 and schedule-window pm-44u3wt remain open with fresh evidence. Next execution begins at plan-step-003, then plan-step-004; preserve every compatibility feature, use SDK contracts first, require negative controls and population adequacy, and add only evidence-backed typed relationships. Complete all-status fuzzy duplicate comparison still fails closed above the million-pair guard under pm-pshhry; exact duplicates remain only the canceled invalid probe trio."
plan_validation[3]{text,command,expected}:
  All-status baseline must remain reproducible and append-only before any terminal enrichment batch.,pm validate --check-history-drift --check-storage-integrity --check-lifecycle --check-resolution --counts --json,"Zero history-chain, storage-integrity, lifecycle, active-blocker, and active-cycle errors; historical metadata debt remains explicitly classified rather than placeholder-normalized."
  Re-run complete tracker graph history metadata duplicate and storage proof after organization and before publication.,pm validate --check-history-drift --check-storage-integrity --check-lifecycle --check-resolution --counts --json && pm graph audit --summary --json && pm graph analyze --summary --json,No history drift storage failure lifecycle cycle missing endpoint duplicate dependency row or new graph finding. Historical metadata warnings remain classified and new milestones are outcome-reachable through typed edges.
  "Post-organization tracker, graph, build, security, changelog, release, and consumer verification completed on the live workspace.","pm validate --check-history-drift --check-storage-integrity --check-lifecycle --check-stale-blockers --dependency-cycle-severity error --parent-cycle-severity error --check-resolution --counts --json && pm graph audit --summary --json && pm graph analyze --summary --json && pm test pm-a8zm --run --progress && pnpm changelog:pm:check","Zero history, storage, lifecycle, dependency, cycle, stale-blocker, graph, build, security, or changelog failures; active outcome reachability complete; historical resolution debt remains classified; npm/npx/bunx resolve the sole daily version."
plan_decisions[3]{ts,author,decision,rationale,evidence}:
  "2026-08-03T11:10:30.966Z","harness:codex","Optimize relationship semantics, reachability, and explainability rather than raw edge density.","The graph is already one connected component with no active isolates. Adding weak related edges would inflate degree while degrading planning, impact, and critical-path meaning.","2026-08-03 graph audit: 10,704 deduplicated directed edges, zero active isolates, 67 redundant edges, ten layers, and only informational legacy findings."
  "2026-08-14T14:37:23.050Z","harness:codex",Extend the outcome ladder beyond universal-domain capability with measured self-improvement federated agent operation and multi-decade continuity.,The existing ladder ended in 2028 while already-canonical programmes explicitly target recursive improvement federation thousands-agent coordination compatibility retention and cryptographic longevity. Outcome milestones make those programme results traversable and evidence-gated without duplicating their implementation scope.,Exact all-status searches found no existing milestone for measured self-improvement federated agent fabric or multi-decade continuity. Created pm-zzylb9 pm-z1kr34 and pm-ljrh29 with typed implementation and verification edges to existing owners.
  "2026-08-15T13:54:29.931Z","harness:codex",Reuse canonical roadmap owners instead of creating new umbrella or algorithm items; add only evidence-backed gaps and semantic graph links.,"Current owners already cover command simplification, output economics, SDK-first parity, adaptive context algorithms, scale, immutable history, multi-agent merge safety, recursive improvement, RL/eval workflows, recurrence gates, provenance, and release reliability through 2036. Placeholder metadata or fabricated relationships would reduce signal and violate lifecycle semantics.","Complete all-status read, full metadata and history census, exact-title scan, active fuzzy scan, graph audit/analyze, targeted owner searches, and live release/provenance inspection."
plan_discoveries[5]{ts,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T11:10:31.658Z","harness:codex","Automatic author harness and instance detection works for current Codex mutations, but model, effort, role, and topic are all explicitly null; corpus-wide topic and role observations remain zero."
  "2026-08-03T11:11:51.782Z","harness:codex","Correction to the preceding provenance discovery: automatic harness and instance detection works for current Codex mutations, whose model, effort, role, and topic are all explicitly null. Across all 43,787 events, model is present on 0, effort on 702, role on 37, and topic on 0; role is sparse, not zero. Immutable history preserves the superseded statement and this correction."
  "2026-08-03T11:29:07.574Z","harness:codex","Fresh hybrid reindex completed, but its checked-in 10-query relevance evaluation failed 6 queries at average nDCG@5 0.7014 while the separately wired 5-query k=10 retrieval CI gate passed at nDCG 0.8327. Canonical owner pm-p1g43q now records the split; future context/retrieval work must converge fixture topology, thresholds, k, and published metrics rather than treating either result as universal."
  "2026-08-14T14:37:22.528Z","harness:codex","Live all-status checkpoint 2026-08-14: 2,489 pre-enrichment items and 49,544 immutable events were read completely with no unreadable records or history drift. The graph had 2,489 recorded nodes and 12,246 deduplicated directed edges in one connected acyclic component with 12 layers and no active isolate. Generic related still represented 45.5 percent while semantic edges represented 7.4 percent. Exact normalized-title review found only the three already-canceled accidental probe duplicates. The built-in duplicate sweep could not execute the all-status corpus because its million-pair safety bound is exceeded and is already owned by pm-pshhry. Strict metadata and linked-file warnings are predominantly historical debt already partitioned into canonical owners and were not placeholder-normalized."
  "2026-08-15T13:54:29.380Z","harness:codex","Live complete inventory on 2026-08-15: 2,495 unique items across 339 open, 2,142 closed, and 14 canceled states; 49,923 history events; 12,287 deduplicated directed graph edges; one connected acyclic component with 12 layers and critical-path length 11. Validation found zero dangling dependencies, cycles, stale blockers, history drift, or storage failures. Active metadata is complete except the intentional roadmap root has no parent. The bounded fuzzy duplicate scan correctly failed closed above one million candidate pairs; exact titles are unique except the previously canceled invalid probe trio."
